---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';
import { formatDate, isoDate } from '../lib/utils';

const crumbs = [
	{ label: 'Home', href: '/' },
	{ label: 'Privacy Policy', href: '/privacy-policy/' },
];

const lastUpdated = new Date('2026-06-20');
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Privacy Policy"
	description="What data GutWise collects, why, how long we keep it and how to have it deleted. Written in plain English — read our full privacy policy."
	schemaNodes={[breadcrumbSchema(crumbs)]}
>
	<PageHeader
		eyebrow="Legal"
		title="Privacy policy"
		intro="Written to be read. If anything here is unclear, ask us and we will explain it — and fix the wording."
		crumbs={crumbs}
	/>

	<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-12">
		<p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
			Last updated{' '}
			<time datetime={isoDate(lastUpdated)}>{formatDate(lastUpdated)}</time>
		</p>

		<div class="prose prose-gutwise mt-8">
			<h2>The short version</h2>
			<p>
				We do not have user accounts and we do not run a database of visitors. The
				only personal information we ever hold is an email address you typed in
				yourself, plus whatever you wrote in a message to us. Analytics cookies
				are off until you accept them. We never sell anything to anyone.
			</p>

			<h2>Who we are</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE.name} publishes educational content about the low-FODMAP diet at{' '}
				<a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>. For any privacy
				question, or to exercise the rights described below, contact{' '}
				<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>What we collect</h2>

			<h3>1. Your email address, if you give it to us</h3>
			<p>
				When you request the Starter Kit, your email address is checked for
				validity and passed straight through to our email service provider. It
				is held in memory only for the moment that takes — this site has no
				database, and nothing is written to disk on our side. The subscriber
				record lives with the provider. We use it to send the download and
				occasional related content, and every email carries a one-click
				unsubscribe link.
				<strong> Lawful basis: consent</strong>, which you can withdraw at any
				time.
			</p>

			<h3>2. Anything you send through the contact form</h3>
			<p>
				Your name, email address, chosen topic and message. These are validated
				and forwarded to our email inbox; nothing is written to a database. We
				keep the message as long as needed to deal with it and then delete it.
				<strong> Lawful basis: legitimate interest</strong> in answering people
				who contact us.
			</p>

			<h3>3. Analytics, only if you accept</h3>
			<p>
				We use two analytics tools, and they behave differently:
			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<strong>Google Analytics 4</strong> — sets cookies, and{' '}
					<strong>is not loaded at all until you press Accept</strong>. This is
					stronger than the common approach: many sites load the Google tag
					immediately and merely tell it not to store cookies, which still sends
					data to Google before you have chosen. We do not fetch the tag until
					you accept. If you decline, no Google code ever runs and nothing is
					stored on your device. <strong>Lawful basis: consent.</strong>
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong> — sets no cookies, uses no
					client-side state and does not fingerprint or track you across sites.
					It counts page views in aggregate. Because it processes no personal
					data, it runs without a consent prompt.{' '}
					<strong>Lawful basis: legitimate interest.</strong>
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h3>4. Server logs</h3>
			<p>
				Our host, Cloudflare, processes standard request data (IP address, user
				agent, requested URL) to serve the site and to protect it from attack and
				abuse. This is ordinary infrastructure logging and we do not use it to
				build any profile of you. <strong>Lawful basis: legitimate interest</strong>{' '}
				in site security and availability.
			</p>

			<h2>What we do not do</h2>
			<ul>
				<li>We do not sell, rent or share your personal data with anyone.</li>
				<li>We do not run advertising cookies or retargeting pixels.</li>
				<li>We have no user accounts, so there are no passwords to leak.</li>
				<li>
					We do not ask for, want, or knowingly store any health information about
					you. Please do not send us medical details — we cannot act on them, and
					we would rather not hold them.
				</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
			<p>
				Only two categories exist on this site. <strong>Analytics cookies</strong>{' '}
				are set by Google Analytics after you accept, and typically last up to two
				years. <strong>Local storage</strong> holds two small values: your cookie
				choice, so we stop asking, and whether you dismissed the mobile banner.
				Neither is sent to any server.
			</p>
			<p>
				To change your mind after choosing, clear this site's data in your
				browser settings and the banner will appear again.
			</p>

			<h2>Affiliate links</h2>
			<p>
				Some outbound links are affiliate links. Following one may allow the
				retailer — most often Amazon — to set their own cookie to attribute a
				purchase to us. That happens on their site and under their privacy policy,
				not ours. We receive only aggregate commission reports and never learn who
				bought what. Our{' '}
				<a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> lists every
				programme we are part of.
			</p>

			<h2>Third parties we rely on</h2>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, CDN, bot protection and cookieless analytics.</li>
				<li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> — consent-gated audience measurement.</li>
				<li><strong>Our email provider</strong> — stores subscriber addresses and sends the Starter Kit.</li>
				<li><strong>Amazon Associates and other affiliate programmes</strong> — purchase attribution on their own sites.</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				If you are in the UK, EU, or a jurisdiction with comparable law, you have
				the right to access the personal data we hold about you, to have it
				corrected or erased, to restrict or object to how we use it, to receive a
				portable copy, and to withdraw consent at any time.
			</p>
			<p>
				In practice this is simple, because we hold very little. Email{' '}
				<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and we will action the
				request within 30 days. Unsubscribing from an email removes you from the
				list immediately without needing to ask us.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you are in the EU or UK, you also have the right to complain to your
				national data protection authority.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>
				This site is intended for adults. We do not knowingly collect personal
				information from anyone under 16. If you believe a child has given us
				their details, contact us and we will delete them.
			</p>

			<h2>Data transfers and security</h2>
			<p>
				Our providers may process data outside your country, including in the
				United States, under standard contractual clauses or equivalent
				safeguards. The site is served over HTTPS with HSTS enforced, and because
				we operate no database and store no credentials, the surface available to
				an attacker is deliberately minimal.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				If we change anything material we will update the date at the top of this
				page. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the
				revised policy.
			</p>

			<h2>Medical disclaimer</h2>
			<p>
				{SITE.name} publishes educational information, not medical advice. See our{' '}
				<a href="/about/">about page</a> for our editorial standards, and always
				consult a qualified healthcare professional before changing your diet.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
